1. CSS fundamentals (Days 1–4)
Day	Topics
1	Introduction to CSS, syntax, selectors
2	Inline, Internal, External CSS
3	Colors, backgrounds, units
4	Text properties, fonts, Google Fonts


Practice projects:
- Personal introduction page
- Stylish heading page
- College information page
2. CSS selectors and box model (Days 5–8)
Topics:
- Element selector
- Class selector
- ID selector
- Universal selector
- Group selector
- Descendant selector
- Child selector
- Pseudo-classes
- Pseudo-elements
- Box model
- Margin, padding, border
- Width and height
- Box-sizing


Mini projects:
1. Profile card
2. Product card
3. Student ID card
4. College faculty profile page
3. CSS layout techniques (Days 9–13)
Learn these concepts carefully because they are important for real-world frontend development.
Topic	What to learn
Display	block, inline, inline-block, none
Position	static, relative, absolute, fixed, sticky
Flexbox	flex-direction, justify-content, align-items
Grid	grid-template-columns, rows, gap
Overflow	hidden, scroll, auto
Z-index	Layer management


Projects:
- Navigation bar
- Responsive image gallery
- Dashboard layout
- E-commerce product grid
4. Advanced CSS (Days 14–18)
Topics:
- Transitions
- Transform
- Animations
- Keyframes
- Gradients
- Box-shadow
- Text-shadow
- Border-radius
- Filters
- Clip-path
- CSS variables
- Custom properties


Projects:
- Animated login page
- Loading animation
- 3D profile card
- Animated landing page
5. Responsive web design (Days 19–22)
Topics:
- Responsive design principles
- Media queries
- Mobile-first approach
- Fluid layouts
- Relative units
- Responsive images
- Flexbox and Grid responsiveness
- CSS breakpoints


Projects:
- Responsive portfolio
- Responsive college website
- Mobile-friendly dashboard
6. Professional CSS (Days 23–25)
Learn:
- CSS architecture
- BEM naming convention
- Reusable components
- CSS specificity
- Inheritance
- CSS debugging using DevTools
- Browser compatibility
- CSS optimization
- CSS frameworks introduction (Bootstrap and Tailwind CSS)

